From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon McGinty <brandon.mcginty@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:22:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] speakup: stop discarding code points above U+FFFF

`synth_writeu` and `speakup_file_writeu` each tested a decoded value
against 0x10000 and dropped the value when the test failed, because the
buffer held a `u16` and could not represent a larger value.  The buffer
now holds a `u32`, so the test has nothing left to protect and only
discards supplementary-plane characters.

Drop both tests.  A supplementary-plane character written to
`/dev/synthu`, or produced by `synth_writeu` on behalf of the virtual
terminal, now reaches the synth buffer intact.

`synth_utf8_get` already rejects a surrogate code point and a value
above U+10FFFF, so no value that reaches `synth_buffer_add` here is
outside Unicode.

Signed-off-by: Brandon McGinty <brandon.mcginty@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/accessibility/speakup/devsynth.c | 3 +--
 drivers/accessibility/speakup/synth.c    | 3 +--
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accessibility/speakup/devsynth.c b/drivers/accessibility/speakup/devsynth.c
index e75394e..543357f 100644
--- a/drivers/accessibility/speakup/devsynth.c
+++ b/drivers/accessibility/speakup/devsynth.c
@@ -74,8 +74,7 @@ static ssize_t speakup_file_writeu(struct file *fp, const char __user *buffer,
 				continue;
 			}
 
-			if (value < 0x10000)
-				ubuf[out++] = value;
+			ubuf[out++] = value;
 		}
 
 		count -= bytes;
diff --git a/drivers/accessibility/speakup/synth.c b/drivers/accessibility/speakup/synth.c
index 504ff0a..475b5e4 100644
--- a/drivers/accessibility/speakup/synth.c
+++ b/drivers/accessibility/speakup/synth.c
@@ -317,8 +317,7 @@ void synth_writeu(const char *buf, size_t count)
 			continue;
 		}
 
-		if (value < 0x10000)
-			synth_buffer_add(value);
+		synth_buffer_add(value);
 	}
 
 	synth_start();
